From: DpadPlay <fernandomlmarques@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: fall back when game root loses its view

Backport the Labwc 0.8.3 behavior to Ubuntu 24.04's Labwc 0.7.1.
Some XWayland games change the root surface to override-redirect, leaving
root->data NULL. Returning NULL makes view_move_to_front() abort. Keep the
live view as the safe root fallback, matching upstream.
---
 src/xwayland.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/xwayland.c b/src/xwayland.c
index 7d276b1..c19859b 100644
--- a/src/xwayland.c
+++ b/src/xwayland.c
@@ -769,6 +769,12 @@ xwayland_view_get_root(struct view *view)
 {
 	struct wlr_xwayland_surface *root = top_parent_of(view);
-	return (struct view *)root->data;
+
+	/*
+	 * XWayland games can set override-redirect on the root surface,
+	 * disassociating it from a view. Keep the mapped child as the root
+	 * fallback instead of returning NULL and aborting while raising it.
+	 */
+	return (root && root->data) ? (struct view *)root->data : view;
 }
 
 static void
